tion":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Sharks beat the Senators 6-2 for their 1st regulation victory of the season","description":"— Colin Graf had a goal and an assist, Yaroslav Askarov stopped 39 shots and the San Jose Sharks beat the Ottawa Senators 6-2 on Thursday night for their first regulation victory of the season.","story":"OTTAWA, Ontario -- — Colin Graf had a goal and an assist, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697394/yaroslav-askarov\">Yaroslav Askarov</a> stopped 39 shots and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/sj/san-jose-sharks\">San Jose Sharks</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/ott/ottawa-senators\">Ottawa Senators</a> 6-2 on Thursday night for their first regulation victory of the season.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874749/nolan-allan\">Nolan Allan</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5550/tyler-toffoli\">Tyler Toffoli</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976839/jacob-trouba\">Jacob Trouba</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874881/zack-ostapchuk\">Zack Ostapchuk</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5361709/ivar-stenberg\">Ivar Stenberg</a> also scored for the Sharks (6-4-1).\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697384/tim-stutzle\">Tim Stutzle</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4588190/jordan-spence\">Jordan Spence</a> scored for Ottawa (7-4-0). <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587815/samuel-ersson\">Samuel Ersson</a> made 23 saves.\n\n\r\n              Ottawa placed goalie <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3069285/linus-ullmark\">Linus Ullmark</a> on injured reserve Thursday after he suffered a lower-body injury a night earlier.\n\n\r\n              Spence scored at 6:24 of the third period to make it a two-goal game.\n\n\r\n              The Senators pulled Ersson while on the power play with under four minutes remaining, but Ostapchuk took advantage of a giveaway and scored an empty-net goal.\n\n\r\n              Stenberg added a second empty-netter to round out the scoring.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Sharks: At Boston on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              Senators: Host the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nyr/new-york-rangers\">New York Rangers</a> on Saturday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-23T02:02:09Z"}}